<title>GERMANY: Brau und Brunnen posts lower 96 sales.</title>
<headline>Brau und Brunnen posts lower 96 sales.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>German brewer Brau und Brunnen said on Friday that its sales dropped by 5.2 percent to around two billion marks in 1996.</p>
<p>The group also said that it had already announced it would post a loss totaling at least 100 million marks for the 1996 business year, adding that extraordinary charges were largely responsible for the loss.</p>
<p>Looking ahead, the group still expects to post an operating loss in 1997 but expects to swing to profit in 1998.</p>
<p>The group added that its beer sales eased by seven percent to 319 million marks last year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
